{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And your strength spent for nothing.</b> Corresponding to ״and it shall yield its produce״ (the third tithe year); and we find the term כוח used of grain, as it says: ״you shall not add לתת כחה to yourself, and it is the fourth year.״" "<b>And your land not give.</b> Corresponding to ״and the land shall give״ — and it is the fifth [year]." "<b>It shall not give its fruit.</b> Corresponding to ״it shall give its fruit״ — and they are two, as Rashi explained."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The comment maps each punishment in the curse to a corresponding blessing from v. 4–5; 'the fourth year' refers to the verse לא תוסף תת כחה לך והיא רביעית, where רביעית = the fourth [year]. The structure is: v. 20c (כחכם) ↔ v. 4c (third-year produce).", 1 "Maps v. 20b (ולא תתן ארצכם) ↔ v. 4b (ונתנה הארץ), the fifth year of the blessing scheme."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:34.816532066Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}